   - Navigate to your repository on GitLab.
   - Click on the "Settings" tab.
   - Scroll down to the "Webhooks" section.

2. **Add a New Webhook**:
   - Click on "Add webhook".
   - Enter the Jenkins URL followed by `/project/your-project-name/webhook/` (e.g., `http://your-jenkins-url/project/your-project-name/webhook/`).
   - Select "Push events" as the trigger.
   - Click "Add webhook".

### Step 2: Configure Jenkins Job

